// 1. build kNN in X for $k=7,15$, RBF affinities $\mathrm{aff}_7,\mathrm{aff}_{15}$
// 2. $Y_a \leftarrow$ t-SNE(perp=30, init=PCA); $Y_b \leftarrow$ t-SNE(perp=30, init=SpectralEmbedding)
// 3. score by k=7 neighbor overlap with high-D, keep best $Y_\star$
// 4. for $t = 1\dots 200$: in $Y$ compute kNN sets $\mathrm{IL}_7,\mathrm{IL}_{15}$ and Cauchy kernel $K = 1/(1+D^2)$
// 5.   $C = (\mathrm{IS}_7\setminus\mathrm{IL}_7)\,\mathrm{aff}_7 - (\mathrm{IL}_7\setminus\mathrm{IS}_7)\,K + 0.2\,(\mathrm{IS}_{15}\setminus\mathrm{IL}_{15})\,\mathrm{aff}_{15}\,K$
// 6.   $g = 2((\sum_j C_{ij})Y - C Y) + 2\lambda(Y - Y_\star)$, step-clip and decay, early stop on stale=40
// 7. return $Y$ with best k=7 overlap

// 1. compute pairwise sq-dist $D$ on $X$, local bandwidths $\sigma_i^{2}$ from k=15 distances
// 2. for each $\rho \in \{0.5,1,2,4\}$: $W^{(\rho)}_{ij} = \exp(-D_{ij}/(\sigma_i\sigma_j\rho^{2}))$, keep top-100 per row
// 3. $W = \sum_\rho \tfrac{1}{\rho} W^{(\rho)}$, symmetrize, build $L_{\mathrm{sym}} = I - D^{-1/2}WD^{-1/2}$
// 4. $Y_0 \leftarrow$ smallest-eigenvector embedding of $L_{\mathrm{sym}}$
// 5. for 100 epochs (Adam lr=0.1): attract along $W$, repel via 500 farthest kNN with weight 0.1
// 6. early-exaggeration 4.0 in first epochs

// 1. build kNN, $\rho_i = $ 1-NN dist, $\sigma_i$ from k=15
// 2. $A_{ij} = \exp(-\max(0, D^{2}_{ij} - \rho_i)/\sigma_i)$, $M_{NN} = A + A^{\top}$ rescaled to mean degree 15
// 3. mid-near $M_{MN}$: per-row pick 5 closest of 10 random; far-pair $M_{FP}$: 20 random non-NN per row
// 4. init $Y \leftarrow$ PCA(2D), normalize
// 5. forces use $K_{NN}=10/(10+D^{2})^{2}$, $K_{MN}=10000/(10000+D^{2})^{2}$, $K_{FP}=1/(1+D^{2})^{2}$
// 6. weight schedule $(w_{NN}, w_{MN}, w_{FP})$: phase A ($t<150$) $w_{MN}$ decays $1000\to 0$, phase B ($150\le t<350$) $(3,2,2)$, phase C ($t\ge 350$) $(4,0,2)$
// 7. Adam (lr=1.0, $\beta=(0.9,0.999)$) for 500 epochs

